---
description: Use absolute nvyr package imports in all Python code.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Python imports

- Import nVyR modules with absolute `nvyr` package paths throughout the project,
  including CLI, daemons, helpers, configuration/operational scripts and tests.
- Use `from nvyr.helpers import interfaces` and `from nvyr.tree import lookup`,
  not relative imports such as `from ..helpers import interfaces`.
- Apply this standard to all new Python code and documentation examples.
- Preserve intentional function-local imports, aliases and import ordering when
  cleaning up existing imports; do not add path manipulation or import fallbacks.
